      "reason": "Since ~2026-10-15 GitHub validates a called reusable workflow against the CALLEE repository's actions.lock at the called SHA and rejects a dependency record whose ref is the bare commit SHA (`Unable to resolve action actions/checkout@3d3c42e5…: invalid lockfile pin`). Every standards commit listed here carries such a record, so every reusable of standards at these revisions dies at `Set up job` for every caller: the run reports `failure` (not startup_failure), the job that dies is the reusable's first one, and the message names an action the caller never wrote.",
