      "replacement": "pin_to_known_good",
      "evidence": [
        "hyperpolymath/cicd-squabbler run 38846539059 (2026-10-16) — first red, byte-identical lock and workflows to the last green run 60e8f7a (2026-10-15)",
        "hyperpolymath/hypatia#929 — five callers re-pinned to 75bd599, jobs created again",
        "hyperpolymath/cicd-squabbler#135 — seven callers re-pinned, lock closure rebuilt from standards' own lock at 75bd599",
        "standards/scripts/lock-selfcheck.sh rates these SELF-CONSISTENT: it checks that every ref is KEYED, not that a key's ref is a tag — this list was produced by a walk of every commit reachable from standards main (1324 commits, 545 with the rejected record shape, 2026-08-19..2026-10-19)"
      ],
      "added": "2026-10-19",
      "added_by": "cicd-suite#54 follow-through (session 01Xn9nqHVbUTRLgBdedoXAc8)",
      "notes": "Keyed on SHA only: standards reusables are pinned by commit, never by tag. The list is a measured window, not a policy about age — a standards commit older than 2026-08-19 has no actions.lock and is NOT in it. Mirrored by gitbot-fleet scripts/lib/stale-reusable-pins.tsv (Window B), which is what fix-stale-reusable-pin.sh rewrites from; regenerate both together when standards fixes or re-breaks a window. 75bd599 is the first commit on standards main whose lock carries no self-SHA action record; the toolchain-input window of June 2026 (rust-ci-reusable only) is WF027 in workflow_audit.ex, not here, because it kills one reusable, not all of them."
    }
